/-!
# The recorded edge pairs generate the actual cut-vertex identifications

Unique oriented incidence identifies the two cut occurrences of each
crossed seam. Vertex-preserving dual walks then connect every pair of
actual triangle corners above one surface vertex. This excludes extra
vertex pinches; equality of projected labels alone would not do so.
-/

